author: codex-agent
comments[12]{created_at,author,text}:
  "2026-10-20T11:14:48.631Z",codex-agent,"Closed pm-todos-chgi fixed the native todos registration only. The legacy alias still has a separate no-input success path and forces mutation mode. The pinned SDK supports arguments/flags metadata, so choose shared native importTodos handler and importContract for both names, preserving file/glob/config options and validation. Add real non-git CLI regression and source/tracker dry-run snapshots, then behavioral revert and full npm/Bun gates at unchanged 97/93/98 thresholds. No SDK limitation forces refusal."
  "2026-10-20T11:17:12.232Z",codex-agent,"Real non-git CLI linked regression passed 1/1 (file argument, file option, glob, section/tags/priority/upsert, no input and missing files, help, source/durable tracker byte preservation). Behavioral revert: kept native handler/contract and tests, restored only the original todos-import registration, rebuilt, then node --test test/legacy-import-cli.test.ts failed 0/1: no input exited 0 and printed the skipping message. Restored the shared handler/contract. Full gates will run with unchanged thresholds and isolated Git identity for npm."
  "2026-10-20T11:39:37.099Z",codex-agent,"After restoring the fix, the linked real CLI regression passed again: 1/1, including source-file and durable tracker preservation. The full npm release gate is running with isolated HOME/Git identity and unchanged 97/93/98 thresholds; typechecking, build and docstrings passed. Existing real-tracker command/ambiguity suites remain active under shared-host contention. No merge or release is being performed."
  "2026-10-20T11:46:27.859Z",codex-agent,"Full npm run release:check passed with isolated HOME, GIT_CONFIG_GLOBAL=/dev/null and GIT_CONFIG_NOSYSTEM=1. Results: 305/305 tests, 0 fail/skip/cancel/todo; canonical-reader acceptance 1/1; coverage lines 97.89, branches 93.95, functions 98.50 above unchanged 97/93/98 thresholds. Packed acceptance passed 4/4: npm-current, bun-current, npm-minimum, bun-minimum. Audit, packaging, changelog, date and provenance checks passed. bun run release:check is now running on unchanged code."
  "2026-10-20T12:03:25.979Z",codex-agent,"Final verification complete: npm run release:check with isolated Git identity and bun run release:check both passed 305/305 tests, canonical-reader 1/1 and packed consumers 4/4, with 0 failures/skips/cancellations/todo. Both measured index.ts coverage 97.89 lines, 93.95 branches and 98.50 functions at unchanged 97/93/98 thresholds. Audit, packaging, changelog, date and provenance passed. Linked real CLI test passed 1/1 after restoring the fix; behavioral revert failed 0/1 on the old zero-exit skip. README commands/Without git guidance and linked file/doc/test evidence are complete. No known implementation risk or SDK input-contract limitation remains; release claim for review without closing."
  "2026-10-20T13:13:47.762Z",codex-agent,"PR 136 review round: fetched all review threads and comments (one unresolved thread, PRRT_kwDOSZpews6uU04z; no pagination remaining). Latest CodeRabbit review has no Outside diff range findings. Verified the POSIX-only extensionless symlink fixture cannot run portably on Windows; add the requested platform skip plus a behavioral Windows simulation that fails before allocating a tracker if setup runs. Whole PR diff self-review found no other instance of this portability defect. Branch already contains origin/main. Published pm version is 2026.10.20; retain the repository-pinned 2026.10.15 host for tracker writes."
  "2026-10-20T13:14:48.698Z",codex-agent,"Behavioral revert proof for PRRT_kwDOSZpews6uU04z: removed only the Windows skip option from the legacy CLI test, keeping the new regression unchanged. node --test test/legacy-import-platform.test.ts failed 0/1 with POSIX fixture setup ran on Windows, proving the real test callback was entered. Restored the guard and the regression passed 1/1. Simulation overrides platform only in a child Node process and makes temp-tracker allocation fail if the fixture runs; the actual CLI fixture still uses the real pinned host and a non-git tracker. dist is ignored and untracked in this repository; build regenerates it locally. npm ci refreshed a merge attribute; restored that unrelated generated change."
  "2026-10-20T13:17:29.968Z",codex-agent,"Both focused regressions passed 2/2, including the real non-git import flow. Auxiliary strict PM health is separate from release:check and reports existing extension host-version skew plus merge-fence drift. Follow-up evidence is recorded on existing certification item pm-todos-zpyc after duplicate searches; retain dependency pins and artifact merge policy in this review round."
  "2026-10-20T13:18:48.715Z",codex-agent,"Linked verification via pm test pm-todos-ztuk --run --progress passed both commands (2/2; real CLI 1/1 and Windows simulation 1/1). Repeated the behavioral revert with the final preload-based regression: removing only the skip option fails 0/1, exit 1, POSIX fixture setup ran on Windows; restoring it passes 1/1. Starting full npm release:check with isolated HOME/Git configuration, followed by bun release:check at unchanged thresholds."
  "2026-10-20T13:53:06.288Z",codex-agent,"Review-round full npm run release:check passed with isolated HOME, GIT_CONFIG_GLOBAL=/dev/null and GIT_CONFIG_NOSYSTEM=1: 306/306 tests, zero failures/skips/cancellations/todo; coverage lines 97.89, branches 93.95, functions 98.50 at unchanged 97/93/98 thresholds. Canonical-reader 1/1; packed consumers 4/4 (npm-current, bun-current, npm-minimum, bun-minimum). Typecheck, docstrings, audit (zero vulnerabilities), packaging, changelog, date and publish-attestation checks all passed. Shared-host load prolonged the first attempt; there were no timeouts or retries. Regenerate changelog after this evidence write, then run the full Bun release gate on unchanged code."
  "2026-10-20T14:07:09.811Z",codex-agent,"Review-round verification complete. npm run release:check with isolated HOME/Git identity and bun run release:check both passed: each 306/306 tests, canonical-reader 1/1, packed consumers 4/4; zero failures/skips/cancellations/todo. Each measured index.ts coverage 97.89 lines, 93.95 branches, 98.50 functions at unchanged 97/93/98 thresholds. Typechecking, docstrings, build/test compilation, production audit (zero vulnerabilities), packaging, changelog, release-date and publish-attestation checks all passed. No timeout or retry was needed. Behavioral skip revert fails 0/1 and restoration passes 1/1; linked PM tests passed 2/2. All unresolved findings were verified and the one valid thread PRRT_kwDOSZpews6uU04z is fixed; no Outside diff range finding was present. Whole PR self-review found no further changed-code instance. Native Windows was simulated rather than run natively. Existing PM health version skew and merge-fence drift are recorded on pm-todos-zpyc; no dependency or telemetry configuration changes were made. Release claim for review without closing."
  "2026-10-21T18:42:40.314Z",codex-agent,"Authorized tracker reconciliation, audit 2026-10-21. Owner-authorized takeover of any historical assignment for this verified terminal transition. Reverified current main 4ae22457fccd: merged #136 (9f5a384); source tree exactly matches the audited snapshot. **Make legacy TODO importer share native input and preview contract.** [PR #136](https://github.com/unbraind/pm-todos/pull/136) (9f5a384) shares native file/glob input and preview/refusal semantics with the legacy todos-import adapter, with real non-Git CLI regressions."
